                        "entry_id": "6c17985e-c2fd-3a55-a75f-00f8d36ae26b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A fool, someone who is out of their senses, simpleton."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Ireland"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "27cafc56-7bed-44c5-bdad-b9fa93528e24",
                                "sense_id": "2d2e2e04-348b-3454-a45e-164029226ad6",
                                "text": "[…] an Omadhaun is a man who began life with some sense, but lost most of it on his journey."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d58003de-6dfd-4c65-b68d-69ff1b88fbeb",
                                "sense_id": "2d2e2e04-348b-3454-a45e-164029226ad6",
                                "text": "It is supposed—they say, you know—to take place in the depot where they get these thundering big country fellows, omadhauns, you know, to drill."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "93225c28-4880-40e8-8637-622226596a08",
                                "sense_id": "2d2e2e04-348b-3454-a45e-164029226ad6",
                                "text": "Tin trumpets some of the omadhauns had brought along to bray with […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d03dc69-bd3b-4d3a-adfd-e0d19e17eb7d",
                                "sense_id": "2d2e2e04-348b-3454-a45e-164029226ad6",
                                "text": "\"No, you omadhaun. It bites your shoulder, rips it right off.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
